# m76.ideal = m75 with the open reordered: C's first pull (carried s1, 2 gt) happens while RP0 is extended (wiggle), M1 [14,30).
# Close right side: s1 spits C to (2,1) (QC: RP0 at (4,0) spits BR home); P3t' spits MR to (3,1); M1's level
# LINE-PUSHES s1 + MR + C (MR and C home) and its QC coupling makes R5 push RP0 home; RP0's long pulse spans M1's
# release (R5's coupled pull fails on the extended RP0), pushing BR to (1,0) and pulling it back.
# Lever trio (use at t0), everything else ideal (redstone blocks behind the pistons, z = -1).
# QC couplings used on purpose: U1 (-2,1) fires U0 (-2,0) below it; M1 (5,1) fires R5 (5,0); carried s1 at (3,1)
# fires RP0 at (3,0); s1 at home fires RP0 once RP0 escaped to (4,0).
